@startuml c4-container
!include <C4/C4_Container>

title C4 Container view — the three roles VDP relates

Person(visitor, "Visitor", "Views a page in an ordinary web browser. Knows nothing about VDP — it only ever receives plain HTML.")

System_Boundary(demo, "golang-vdp-demo") {
  Container(bff, "BFF", "Go · net/http", "The VDP client. Runs the §8 resolution algorithm — extract descriptor, fetch it, fetch the root template, recurse into slots, render — and returns HTML (§7.5).")
  Container(api, "API", "Go · net/http", "Returns data with a view descriptor attached (§4), serves standalone descriptor resources (§5), and advertises discovery + the trusted allowlist (§13).")
  Container(templates, "Template server", "Go · net/http", "Serves templates as cacheable resources, fetched by URL like any other resource (§5.2).")
}

Rel(visitor, bff, "Requests a page", "HTTP")
Rel_Back(visitor, bff, "Plain HTML")
Rel(bff, api, "Discovery, then data + view descriptor", "HTTP (§4, §5, §13)")
Rel(bff, templates, "Fetches templates by URL, trusted-allowlist checked", "HTTP (§5.2, §10)")

note as N
  In this demo the three containers run in **one Go process** and talk to each
  other over real HTTP. In production they would be separate deployments — the
  template server a CDN or git host, the API its own backend — which is exactly
  the separation VDP is designed around.
end note

SHOW_LEGEND()
@enduml
